A||||5||Shiner||Interior questions!||||5||
Z||000000||Shiner||02-16-2000||03:21 AM||||Okay, so the interior in my project GT is pretty thrashed.  All the carpet is going.  Wheel needs to be replaced, or recovered.  Dash corners are boffed up.  Anyway, I need to know if it is possible to remove the seat belts and install better condition junkyard ones!  <P> I am also trying to think up a color scheme for the interor (tan, with two-tone dash).  I am doing ALL the carpet, and the seats, with Mr. Mike's stuff.  What do you think about all black carpets, with some kind of tan seat?  <P> Can I really die/paint the plastic trim pieces or dash in the car black, and have a durable, glossy finish?  <P> Thanks guys!||||reg||5
Z||000001||JetroGT||02-16-2000||05:16 AM||||Rip out all the bad stuff. Find a good dash and repaint it with some plastic paint. It dosen't matter what year it's from. Be sure to degrease it first to get rid of any plastic treatment. Carpet is easy. If the padding is good, save it. The seat belts are held in by some torx bolts. One near the roof, and one near the floor. Be carfel not to break the plastic cover on the top torx. Once you remove the bolts you can remove the panel and get at the retractor which are also held in by torx bolts. Have fun. ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-16-2000||05:24 AM||||Mr. Mikes says to leave the original carpet in, pull the jute backing off of his and install over the original.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||02-16-2000||07:21 AM||||Don't yell at me too much but I looked at a Miata interior and was struck by the color combo. They had black carpet tan seats and black and tan dash, car was yellow. I think I'm going to use the same combo for my Lambo when I get that far. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||02-16-2000||09:54 AM||||Keep in mind that black carpet will show EVERYTHING. I have black carpet in my 69 Firebird. I only drive it a once or twice a week and it needs to be vacuumed everytime or it looks dirty. But, it does look good when it's clean.<P>my $0.02 worth,<BR>Roy L.||||reg||4
Z||000005||Eric||02-16-2000||08:33 PM||||That's true, but it never looks stained like the gray carpet.<BR>||||reg||1
